            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Hoot Williams"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is an excellent recipe. It is a fluffy and moist sponge-type cake with a rich, yeasty flavor. Notes: #1: I added 1 tsp. of sugar to the 1/2 cup of warm water to dissolve the 2 tsps. of yeast. Otherwise, it would not activate and become foamy. #2: I lined the steamer basket with parchment paper and omitted the cake pan (as pictured). #3: I used 1/4 cup of my favorite raisins, \"Trader Joe's Jumbo Raisin Medley\" roughly chopped into smaller pieces.",
